@startuml sql-engine-logical-plan
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam component {
  BorderColor #534AB7
  BackgroundColor #EEEDFE
  FontColor #26215C
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888780
  BackgroundColor #F1EFE8
  FontColor #2C2C2A
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #888780
  BackgroundColor #F1EFE8
  FontColor #2C2C2A
}

title labukDB — SQL Engine Architecture, Phase 1 (core.logical)\nCopyright 2026 Afzal and lakehouse-flight contributors — Apache 2.0

legend top left
  |= color |= meaning |
  |<#EEEDFE>| built this session (Phase 1) |
  |<#F1EFE8>| unchanged, reused as-is |
endlegend

[SqlQueryTranslator\n(jsqlparser-based -- a real SQL\ngrammar, not hand-rolled. Already\nparses JOIN/subquery syntax fine;\nTHIS class explicitly rejects them\npost-parse, lines 93-100 -- not a\ngrammar limitation)] as SQTR #F1EFE8
[SqlQuery\n(flat record: table, columns,\npredicate, groupBy, aggregates,\norderBy, limit)] as SQQ #F1EFE8

[LogicalPlanBuilder.build()] as LPB #EEEDFE
[RuleBasedOptimizer.DEFAULT\n.optimize()] as RBO #EEEDFE
[LogicalPlanExecutor.resolve(\nplan, format, dataFileRoot,\nversion, asOf)] as LPE #EEEDFE
[ResolvedScan\n(files, columns, aggregate,\nsort, limit, snapshot metadata)] as RS #EEEDFE

SQTR --> SQQ : translate(sql)
SQQ --> LPB
LPB --> RBO
RBO --> LPE
LPE --> RS

rectangle "Tree shape BEFORE optimization\n(LogicalPlanBuilder's output, one Project\nalways wraps the whole thing)" as BEFORE #FFFFFF {
  rectangle "Project(columns)" as B1 {
    rectangle "Limit(n)" as B2 {
      rectangle "Sort(sortKeys)" as B3 {
        rectangle "Aggregate(groupBy, aggregates)" as B4 {
          rectangle "Filter(predicate)" as B5 {
            rectangle "TableScan(name, null, null)" as B6
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

rectangle "Tree shape AFTER optimization\n(PushFilterIntoScan absorbs Filter;\nPushProjectIntoScan absorbs + drops Project)" as AFTER #FFFFFF {
  rectangle "Limit(n)" as A1 {
    rectangle "Sort(sortKeys)" as A2 {
      rectangle "Aggregate(groupBy, aggregates)" as A3 {
        rectangle "TableScan(name, predicate, requestedColumns)" as A4
      }
    }
  }
}

RBO .down.> AFTER : produces
LPB .down.> BEFORE : produces

note bottom of AFTER
  Only nodes the query actually used survive
  -- e.g. a plain "SELECT x FROM t" optimizes
  straight down to one bare TableScan, nothing
  wrapping it at all. requestedColumns is the
  EXACT union QueryCommand used to compute
  inline before this rule existed: group-by +
  aggregate-input columns when aggregating,
  else SELECT list + ORDER BY columns.
  WHERE-only columns need no explicit handling
  -- ParquetToArrowReader already unions
  predicate columns in at decode time.
end note

note right of LPE
  Deliberately does NOT open the table itself.
  Format detection (Delta vs. Iceberg vs.
  REST-catalog Iceberg) needs cross-module
  visibility into labukdb-format-iceberg that
  labukdb-core doesn't have. QueryCommand (in
  labukdb-cli, which depends on both modules)
  resolves the table name into an already-open
  TableFormat + the TableLocation its data
  files resolve against, FIRST, then hands
  both in here. This class's job starts at
  snapshot resolution (format.latest()/
  atVersion()/atTimestamp()) and ends at
  "files to scan" -- the genuinely
  format-agnostic part.

  Real gap found + fixed to make this true:
  DeltaTableFormat existed but only had a
  local-only Path constructor -- would have
  silently broken MinIO Delta SQL queries if
  wired in naively. Added
  DeltaTableFormat(TableLocation), delegating
  to the already-remote-capable
  SnapshotManager.forLocation.
end note

[QueryCommand.runSql] as QC #F1EFE8
[needsCombine()?\n(aggregate/sort/limit present)] as DECISION #FFF1CF
[CombinedQueryExecutor.execute(...)\n(unchanged, reused as-is)] as CQE #F1EFE8
[scanAndPrintAllFiles(...)\n(new -- unified per-file streaming,\nboth formats now, not just Delta)] as STREAM #EEEDFE
[printHeader + printRows\n+ exact row count] as OUT1 #F1EFE8
[printHeader + printRows\nper file, no cap] as OUT2 #EEEDFE

RS --> QC
QC --> DECISION
DECISION --> CQE : true
DECISION --> STREAM : false
CQE --> OUT1
STREAM --> OUT2

note bottom of STREAM
  Deliberate, named behavioral improvement,
  not a silent regression: Iceberg's CLI path
  previously ALWAYS went through
  CombinedQueryExecutor regardless of whether
  the query aggregated/sorted/limited
  (IcebergTableFormat's own javadoc had
  flagged this as non-ideal). Now streams
  per-file for a plain SELECT on EITHER
  format, matching Delta's existing smarter
  behavior -- lower memory, identical output.
end note

note as SCOPE
  <b>Scope boundaries, explicit:</b>
  - Flight (LabukDbFlightProducer) untouched --
    its own JSON query protocol is a separate,
    pre-decomposed shape, never SQL text.
    Mapping it onto this same LogicalPlan is
    natural future work, not done here.
  - Predicate gains no new node types this
    phase -- no NOT, no cross-column comparison
    (every leaf is still "column OP literal").
  - CombinedQueryExecutor/AggregateOperator/
    SortLimitOperator are not decomposed into
    individually-pluggable physical operators
    yet -- needed once a Join operator has to
    sit between scan and aggregate (Phase 3).

  <b>The arc beyond this phase:</b>
  Phase 2 -- more optimizer rules.
  Phase 3 -- joins: needs Predicate extended
  with cross-column comparisons (t1.a = t2.b),
  a new Join physical operator, and
  SqlQueryTranslator actually walking
  plainSelect.getJoins() instead of rejecting it.
  Phase 4 -- subqueries (scalar, IN (SELECT...),
  EXISTS).
end note

@enduml
